<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20936] llite: allow disabling cgroup writeback (SB_I_CGROUPWB) on client mounts</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20936</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Lustre clients always set &lt;tt&gt;SB_I_CGROUPWB&lt;/tt&gt; on the superblock (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16697" title="Lustre should set appropriate BDI_CAP_* and s_iflags for writeback and cgroup wb" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16697"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16697&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16954" title="mount failed: File exists(cannot create duplicate filename '/devices/virtual/bdi/lustre-ffffxxx')" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16954"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16954&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;). As a result, every inode a cgroup dirties is attached to that cgroup's writeback context.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a cgroup is removed (for example when a container exits), the kernel has to switch all of those inodes back to a parent writeback context in &lt;tt&gt;inode_switch_wbs_work_fn()&lt;/tt&gt;. On clients with a very large inode cache this produces a large number of CPU-hogging work items that contend on &lt;tt&gt;wb-&amp;gt;list_lock&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;workqueue: inode_switch_wbs_work_fn hogged CPU for &amp;gt;10000us N times, consider switching to WQ_UNBOUND
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We have seen this stall the client node's kernel workqueues for minutes, with hung kworkers. During the stall the client stopped pinging, was ping-evicted by all targets, and discarded dirty pages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Newer kernels reduce the cost of the switching ("writeback: Avoid contention on wb-&amp;gt;list_lock when switching inodes" and related patches, v6.18). On older kernels, though, Lustre gives no way to opt out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Proposal:&lt;/b&gt; add client mount options &lt;tt&gt;cgroupwb&lt;/tt&gt; (default, current behaviour) and &lt;tt&gt;nocgroupwb&lt;/tt&gt;, which skips setting &lt;tt&gt;SB_I_CGROUPWB&lt;/tt&gt; so inodes stay on the bdi root writeback context. The trade-off is that dirty throttling becomes system-wide rather than per cgroup (see &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16713" title="Writeback and commit pages under memory pressure to avoid OOM" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16713"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16713&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;). A patch will follow.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
